# Normalize line endings so `gofmt -l .` stays a meaningful gate.
#
# Why this matters: gofmt rewrites CRLF to LF. If a Windows contributor clones
# this repo with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) and saves a
# .go file, Git hands back a CRLF file, gofmt then lists every single one, and
# the CI formatting gate fails on code that is otherwise correct. Pinning
# eol=lf in the index makes the working tree agree with gofmt on every OS.
#
# Rules are listed per file type on purpose. A blanket `* text=auto` would make
# Git guess for every file, including any future binary asset, and can corrupt
# files it guesses wrong about. Only the text types this repo actually uses are
# pinned here.

# Go source and test files - governed by the gofmt gate in CI.
*.go text eol=lf

# CI workflow definitions
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Documentation
*.md text eol=lf

# Project config files
.gitignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf
